Comment (internal/api/handler/agent_config_sync.go:186):
**[Blocker] Report fields are truncated before secrets are masked, so part of a secret can leak**

`normalizeReport` (line 167) cuts `error` to 8 KiB, warning messages and paths to 1 KiB, `unsafe[].value` to 2 KiB and plugin sources to 2 KiB. `scrubReportText` only runs here, afterwards. A secret that straddles the cut no longer matches any pattern, so its prefix is stored and returned to every `agent:read` holder (viewers, under Cedar).

Checked against `containsSecretValue`:
- `"dial postgres://app:hunter2secretpw@db:5432/x"` is masked;
- the same string cut to `"dial postgres://app:hunter2se"` is **not** masked.

**Why:** Masking must see the full value. Once it's truncated, the URL/userinfo and token patterns can't recognise it.
**Fix:** Scrub before truncating: call `scrubReportText(&report)` before `normalizeReport`, or move the scrub into `normalizeReport` ahead of the length caps. A masked value is exactly `••••`, so the caps then only apply to values that aren't secret. Add a unit test with a URL password across the 8 KiB `error` cut and across the 1 KiB warning-message cut.
**Severity basis:** no rule matched; decision tree: security, data or released-contract risk.

